Why Floci?

Floci provides an AWS-compatible local environment that allows developers to interact with AWS-style APIs locally.

The project documentation describes Floci as an open-source local cloud emulator that can be used without an AWS account or cloud billing.

Floci supports a large collection of AWS services and uses the same general AWS API interaction model, allowing applications and automation tools to communicate with the local environment.

Zero-Cost Development

One of the primary objectives of this project is eliminating unnecessary AWS cloud costs during development and experimentation.

Instead of:
Developer
    │
    ▼
AWS Account
    │
    ▼
Billable Resources
    │
    ▼
Monthly Cloud Cost
we use:
Developer
    │
    ▼
Docker
    │
    ▼
Floci
    │
    ▼
Local AWS Environment
    │
    ▼
$0 Cloud Infrastructure Cost

This makes it possible to repeatedly destroy and recreate infrastructure without worrying about cloud charges.

